#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:13
msgid "PARA Memory Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:15
msgid ""
"Persistent, file-based memory organized by Tiago Forte's PARA method. "
"Three layers: a knowledge graph, daily notes, and tacit knowledge. All "
"paths are relative to `$AGENT_HOME`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:17
msgid "Three Memory Layers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:19
msgid "Layer 1: Knowledge Graph (`$AGENT_HOME/life/` -- PARA)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:21
msgid "Entity-based storage. Each entity gets a folder with two tiers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:23
msgid "`summary.md` -- quick context, load first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:24
msgid "`items.yaml` -- atomic facts, load on demand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:41
msgid "**PARA rules:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:43
msgid ""
"**Projects** -- active work with a goal or deadline. Move to archives "
"when complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:44
msgid "**Areas** -- ongoing (people, companies, responsibilities). No end date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:45
msgid "**Resources** -- reference material, topics of interest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:46
msgid "**Archives** -- inactive items from any category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:48
msgid "**Fact rules:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:50
msgid "Save durable facts immediately to `items.yaml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:51
msgid "Weekly: rewrite `summary.md` from active facts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:52
msgid ""
"Never delete facts. Supersede instead (`status: superseded`, add "
"`superseded_by`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:53
msgid ""
"When an entity goes inactive, move its folder to "
"`$AGENT_HOME/life/archives/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:55
msgid "**When to create an entity:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:57
msgid "Mentioned 3+ times, OR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:58
msgid "Direct relationship to the user (family, coworker, partner, client), OR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:59
msgid "Significant project or company in the user's life."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:60
msgid "Otherwise, note it in daily notes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:62
msgid ""
"For the atomic fact YAML schema and memory decay rules, see "
"[references/schemas.md](references/schemas.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:64
msgid "Layer 2: Daily Notes (`$AGENT_HOME/memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:66
msgid "Raw timeline of events -- the \"when\" layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:68
msgid "Write continuously during conversations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:69
msgid "Extract durable facts to Layer 1 during heartbeats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:71
msgid "Layer 3: Tacit Knowledge (`$AGENT_HOME/MEMORY.md`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:73
msgid "How the user operates -- patterns, preferences, lessons learned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:75
msgid "Not facts about the world; facts about the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:76
msgid "Update whenever you learn new operating patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:78
msgid "Write It Down -- No Mental Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:80
msgid "Memory does not survive session restarts. Files do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:82
msgid "Want to remember something -> WRITE IT TO A FILE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:83
msgid ""
"\"Remember this\" -> update `$AGENT_HOME/memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` or the "
"relevant entity file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:84
msgid "Learn a lesson -> update AGENTS.md, TOOLS.md, or the relevant skill file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:85
msgid "Make a mistake -> document it so future-you does not repeat it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:86
msgid "On-disk text files are always better than holding it in temporary context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:88
msgid "Memory Recall -- Use qmd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:90
msgid "Use `qmd` rather than grepping files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:98
msgid "Index your personal folder: `qmd index $AGENT_HOME`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:100
msgid "Vectors + BM25 + reranking finds things even when the wording differs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:102
msgid "Planning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/para-memory-files_SKILL.md:104
msgid ""
"Keep plans in timestamped files in `plans/` at the project root (outside "
"personal memory so other agents can access them). Use `qmd` to search "
"plans. Plans go stale -- if a newer plan exists, do not confuse yourself "
"with an older version. If you notice staleness, update the file to note "
"what it is supersededBy."
msgstr ""

